A Production Readiness Assessment evaluates whether an Azure solution is fully prepared for live production workloads. It verifies that technical, operational, and business requirements have been satisfied before deployment.

The assessment generally covers:

* Infrastructure readiness
* Security validation
* Monitoring configuration
* Backup and recovery
* High availability
* Disaster recovery
* Documentation
* Support ownership
* Capacity planning

For example, before launching a nationwide banking portal, administrators verify that every production dependency has been tested and documented.

A real-life use case is preventing production failures by identifying missing configurations before deployment.

Production readiness assessments significantly improve deployment confidence.
